[{"id":"VRCE-7-84-1","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":84,"verse":1,"english":"That sacrifice, the like of which was never seen before, having been undertaken the illustrious ascetic Valmiki, with his disciples, came there.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.621,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-93-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7084001","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"53d60dc2d37e4d1de7f9f849297ef7a4222b27c5e6cb801ba0cc0d888e51a2ca","compact":"b41a2895c9686d2cddbadbdbb1406e6e3251a14123b044410d57ea9a49c8cd3c","nasal":"b41a2895c9686d2cddbadbdbb1406e6e3251a14123b044410d57ea9a49c8cd3c"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-84-2","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":84,"verse":2,"english":"And beholding this wonderful sacrifice resembling that of the celestials, his followers, the Rşis, made charming cottages in a solitary corner and at no distance.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.587,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-93-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7084002","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0bddff227136e4fdc38a69c70b4624ebb62dce5118890babe9001a9995385155","compact":"e77942b44d99d03df4bd029a4b32e913232bac79a8b279e4b827431debdbf0a6","nasal":"1e5cbdecaef167b40dd9386e4c126ed1e02154d7398487cac14d1c6d48d40e78"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-84-3","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":84,"verse":3,"english":"There upon Vālmīki said to his disciples, Lava and Kuća Do you carefully and delightedly sing the whole of Rāmāyaṇa in the highly holy hermitages, of the Rşis, in the homes where perpetual fire is kept up by the Brāhmaṇas, in streets and palaces, at the gate of Rāma's house, in the sacrificial arena and before all Rtvik.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.879,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-93-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskri